WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.083 --> 00:00:03.629
Mom! I'm going to a wedding!

00:00:04.213 --> 00:00:05.297
Female:
It could have been anyone.

00:00:05.297 --> 00:00:06.423
(Travis screaming)

00:00:06.423 --> 00:00:07.424
(music)

00:00:07.424 --> 00:00:09.051
Grace killed them both

00:00:09.510 --> 00:00:10.510
(Grace screaming)

00:00:11.053 --> 00:00:13.055
That is hea-vy!

00:00:13.055 --> 00:00:14.723
(music)

00:00:14.723 --> 00:00:18.268
I was surprised at how quickly
they were able to solve all the
little puzzles last season.

00:00:18.268 --> 00:00:20.771
Christopher Miller:
People would freeze frame and
re-watch.

00:00:21.230 --> 00:00:23.523
It's time to party!

00:00:23.649 --> 00:00:26.902
It's what season two is all
about. It all adds up to
something.

00:00:26.902 --> 00:00:27.819
Aha!

00:00:27.819 --> 00:00:32.032
I didn't catch on to any of the
puzzles except for when the did
something on the [bleeped out]

00:00:32.032 --> 00:00:33.200
It's nothing nasty.

00:00:33.492 --> 00:00:36.495
Seeing the forums that sprung up
ten minutes after an episode
came out.

00:00:36.495 --> 00:00:39.331
They would have found the
puzzle, solved the puzzle, and
then be arguing about it.

00:00:39.331 --> 00:00:40.332
Press "Input".

00:00:40.332 --> 00:00:41.250
(Everyone arguing over each
other)

00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:42.251
You know what? Shut up!

00:00:42.459 --> 00:00:43.794
Christopher Miller:
If you are a casual viewer, 

00:00:43.794 --> 00:00:46.004
you shouldn’t be able to figure
it out easily.

00:00:46.171 --> 00:00:47.214
Help me mommy.

00:00:47.256 --> 00:00:48.340
Christopher Miller:
But the clues are there.

00:00:48.924 --> 00:00:51.134
Elizabeth Perkins:
There’s clues in words, clues in
paintings...

00:00:51.134 --> 00:00:52.636
There's so many clues.

00:00:52.678 --> 00:00:54.137
Not a difficult puzzle to solve.

00:00:54.429 --> 00:00:55.514
David Kwong:
Chris came to us and said,

00:00:55.514 --> 00:00:57.099
I wanna add a bunch of other
layers.

00:00:57.182 --> 00:00:58.850
David Kwong:
What can we put on the wall?

00:00:58.850 --> 00:01:00.227
David Kwong:
What can we have people saying?

00:01:00.269 --> 00:01:01.395
David Kwong:
What can we have people wearing?

00:01:01.770 --> 00:01:03.105
Dave Shukan:
In After Party one,

00:01:03.105 --> 00:01:05.274
It was one puzzle per episode.

00:01:05.357 --> 00:01:05.649
-Shock!

00:01:05.649 --> 00:01:09.236
There are more puzzles this
season and they are far more
difficult.

00:01:09.319 --> 00:01:11.697
And that meant hiding two things
in every episode.

00:01:12.364 --> 00:01:15.284
What could we put on each table
that might be puzzles?

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:16.702
I-I gotta walk this off.

00:01:17.202 --> 00:01:19.079
Christopher Miller:
It was a gauntlet thrown this
season 

00:01:19.079 --> 00:01:21.790
Christopher Miller:
to have even more twists
and even more puzzles.

00:01:21.957 --> 00:01:22.916
Let’s have some fun!

00:01:22.916 --> 00:01:23.292
-Slap

00:01:23.292 --> 00:01:23.750
-Slap

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:24.209
(Music plays)
-Slap

00:01:24.251 --> 00:01:24.960
♪♪

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:25.669
Christopher Miller:
And that’s the trick.

00:01:25.669 --> 00:01:27.170
Christopher Miller:
Have a mystery that’s engaging

00:01:27.170 --> 00:01:29.172
Christopher Miller:
or people who are just casually
watching,

00:01:29.214 --> 00:01:31.008
and the people who are really
intensely watching.

00:01:31.049 --> 00:01:31.591
♪♪

00:01:31.591 --> 00:01:34.428
Man:
After party in the library!

00:01:34.428 --> 00:01:35.637
(Everyone cheers!)

00:01:35.679 --> 00:01:38.307
♪♪

00:01:38.348 --> 00:01:40.017
All the secrets are coming out.

00:01:40.183 --> 00:01:41.184
Time to get squiffy.

00:01:41.184 --> 00:01:41.518
(Cork-pops)

